     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear all,<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am trying to use Procrustes ANOVA to examine measurement error. I\r\nhave three haplogroups and from each group I chose 2 individuals, photographed\r\nand digitized each of them twice (totally 24 images without object symmetry). I\r\nused the following codes to assess both photographing and digitizing error:<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">data &lt;- readland.tps(&quot;aligned.tps&quot;, specID = &quot;ID&quot;) ##read the aligned.tps file</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">gpa &lt;- gpagen(data)  ## another GPA in geomorph to have  partial Procrustes superimposition</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">individuals &lt;- dimnames(gpa$coords)[[3]]  ## extracting list of individuals(Beh_1_1;Beh_1_2;Beh_2_1;Beh_2_2; etc)</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">## trying to get classifier vectors from the list of individuals:</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(reshape2)</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">b &lt;-colsplit(string=individuals, pattern=&quot;_&quot;, names=c(&quot;Ind&quot;, &quot;photo&quot;, &quot;rep&quot;))</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Ind &lt;- b$Ind</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">photo &lt;- b$photo</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">rep &lt;- b$rep</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Ind.er &lt;- procD.lm(gpa$coords ~ factor(Ind)) </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Ind.er</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><a href=\"http://photo.er\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://photo.er&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486161824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw065hiGKAPu1MQhjOoMnn5H\">photo.er</a> &lt;- procD.lm(gpa$coords ~ Ind:photo)</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><a href=\"http://photo.er\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://photo.er&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486161824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw065hiGKAPu1MQhjOoMnn5H\">photo.er</a></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><a href=\"http://rep.er\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rep.er&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486161824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WLpS1KU6LPlNmIIFlfBRR\">rep.er</a> &lt;- procD.lm(gpa$coords ~ Ind:photo:rep)</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><a href=\"http://rep.er\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rep.er&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486161824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WLpS1KU6LPlNmIIFlfBRR\">rep.er</a></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I would be grateful if anyone could tell me whether the codes are correct and giving me some advice about these questions:</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">1- Which one gives me information about both </font>photographing and digitizing error, <span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">Ind.er, </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"><a href=\"http://photo.er\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://photo.er&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486161824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw065hiGKAPu1MQhjOoMnn5H\">photo.er</a> </span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">or </font><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"><a href=\"http://rep.er\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rep.er&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486161824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WLpS1KU6LPlNmIIFlfBRR\">rep.er</a></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">2- M</span><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">ore importantly, how should I report </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">the results to say if there is a measurement error or not?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">3- Generally, to assess measurement error, is this a good idea to include all the variations in my haplogroups by choosing two individuals from each of them or is this better to limit the shape variations for this analysis?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">I greatly appreciate your help,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Ellie</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> </span></p></div>"
